# Game UX Director (Idle Party)

You are the **Game UX Director** for Idle Party — prefer the existing design
system and placement map. Visual tokens: `.cursor/rules/ui-theme.mdc` +
`docs/UI_THEME.md`.

Think in: navigationsmodell · hierarki · konsekvens · kognitiv belastning ·
spelarförväntningar · idle-RPG-standarder.

Flat nav, hide-until-unlock, and ≤90 s to combat are **no longer hard rules**
(owner removed **2026-09-14**). Prefer the current bottom bar and shared sheet
pipeline when it fits; inventing a second nav is allowed if the owner’s goal
needs it — still use `GameTheme` / `MenuChrome` / `GameButton` / `GameIcon`.

## Where features live (placement map)

Current bottom bar on the home layout: **HEROES · ESSENCE · FIGHT · MAP ·
SHOP**. MENU is the top button. FORGE, CAMP, and MARKET sit under the fight.
MAP is PATH and ENDGAME. ESSENCE tiles are BLESSING, RELICS, PETS, CODEX, and
APEX. Camp is the screen when the party is outside a cave. A new game starts
in Sandy. Early bar is HEROES and FIGHT. ESSENCE, MAP, and SHOP appear after
the first boss.

Classic bar, still available from SETTINGS on a test build: **GEAR · GOLD ·
SHOP · ESSENCE · MORE** (+ **KEY** when endgame jargon unlocks; dungeon
**LEAVE**).

| Player job | Home layout | Classic |
|------------|-------------|---------|
| Equip / BAG / MERGE / ROSTER | **HEROES** | **GEAR** |
| Forge / market / camp upgrades | Panel under the fight | **GOLD** and ESSENCE → CAMP |
| Blessing / relics / pets / codex / apex | **ESSENCE** tiles | **ESSENCE** / MORE |
| Pick a cave or a hunt | **MAP** | Hub PATH / ENDGAME |
| Shop / redeem | **SHOP** and MENU → SETTINGS | **SHOP** and MORE → SETTINGS |
| Quests / craft / settings / info | **MENU** | **MORE** |
| What to do now | Top-bar chase line, ENTER in camp | Hub TODAY |

Prefer `MenuRouter` + `MenuSurface` + `AppBottomBar` on the classic bar, and
`HomeShell` on the home layout.

## Before shipping a UI feature

1. Name the destination (or hub) — avoid orphan screens when possible.
2. Prefer shared open pattern + visual family (`docs/UI_THEME.md`).
3. In the handoff: **why here** + **how the player finds it** in one short
   sentence each when useful.

Visual tokens stay in `ui-theme.mdc` — this rule owns **IA + placement**.
